bbreviation_in_the_article":9,"value":2.14,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1021/acs.inorgchem.3c00757","year":2023,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000732","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"Lipophilicity of the complexes was evaluated by standard shake-flask method. Octanolwater (1:1 v/v) mixture was used in the study. Solutions (50 μM) of complexes 1-12 were prepared using octanol saturated water and treated with equal amount of water-octanol mixture. The mixture was kept for shaking for 24 h. After the separation of two layers, the absorbance values were evaluated using electronic spectroscopy. The log Po/w values were calculated using the equation, log Po/w = log (Corg/Caq), where Corg refers to the concentration of complexes in organic layer and Caq refers to the concentration in aqueous layer."}]}